# Translation files
#
# translations/en.json is the hand-written source of truth — edit it, then run
# `python scripts/sync_keys.py`, which regenerates every other language file.
# Those generated files are committed (so the Docker build stays offline and
# reproducible) but their diffs are noise: one key added to en.json rewrites all
# 12 of them.
#
#   linguist-generated=true  -> GitHub collapses them in PR diffs
#   -diff                    -> local `git diff` prints "Binary files differ"
#                               instead of thousands of lines
#
# Content is still tracked normally, so `git diff --exit-code` in CI and text
# merges both keep working. To inspect one by hand: git diff --text <file>
translations/*.json   linguist-generated=true -diff

# ...except English, which is written by humans and must stay reviewable.
translations/en.json  linguist-generated=false diff

# Worksheets: the PDFs and the markdown sheets are content, not code. GitHub
# collapses their diffs in PRs ("Load diff"); local `git diff` is unchanged.
*.pdf                              linguist-generated=true
seed/files/content/worksheets/**   linguist-generated=true
data/worksheets/**                 linguist-generated=true

# Shell scripts run inside the Linux image. With core.autocrlf=true on Windows
# both checkouts and `git archive` (local-forge/deploy.ps1) would write CRLF,
# and /bin/sh fails on `set -e\r` before gunicorn starts.
*.sh  text eol=lf
